return {
["23:00"]={"Two hours passed slowly away, and then, suddenly, just at the stroke of \003eleven\004, a single bright light shone out right in front of us.","The Adventures of Sherlock Holmes","Sir Arthur Conan Doyle"},
["23:01"]={"I gazed at him. then, as it dawned on me that he wasn’t joking, I looked at all the little clocks on the kitchen appliances. They all agreed: \003one minute past eleven\004.","Dying for Millions","Judith Cutler"},
["23:02"]={"“Yes.” Perena’s firm tone brooked no argument. “It exploded at 11:07. You would have entered at \00311:02\004, so that by then you would have been exactly midway between the Gates.”","The Shadow and Night","Chris Walley"},
["23:04"]={"He came out of his reverie and noticed on the digital clock that it was already \003four minutes past eleven\004. As he began switching channels, he cursed himself, cursed his weakness, and cursed the satanic forces that were loose in this accursed land.","The Lion’s Game","Nelson DeMille"},
["23:05"]={"\003Five past eleven\004; less than a quarter of an hour before Amethyst either succeeded or failed","The Infinite Day","Chris Walley"},
["23:06"]={"He looked at the large clock on the wall and saw that it was \003six minutes past eleven o’clock\004, local time. That was as it should have been.","Lightning","Dean Koontz"},
["23:07"]={"“Yes.” Perena’s firm tone brooked no argument. “It exploded at \00311:07\004. You would have entered at 11:02, so that by then you would have been exactly midway between the Gates.”","The Shadow and Night","Chris Walley"},
["23:08"]={"He glanced up so that he could see the time on the datastrip along the upper edge of his helmet: \00311:08\004:23. Ten minutes. They walked unsteadily on.","The Infinite Day","Chris Walley"},
["23:09"]={"The time is \00311:09\004 at that point, Powell said to the D.A.’s staff. “Watch the clock above the model. It’s geared to synchronize with the slow motion.”\nIn rapt silence, the legal division studied the scene and jotted notes while the androids reproduced the actions of the fatal Beaumont party.","The Demolished Man","Alfred Bester"},
["23:10"]={"She backed down the driveway, checked for traffic, and turned toward the turnpike. \003Ten past eleven\004. Plenty of time.\nThat’s what she thought then.","If It Bleeds","Stephen King"},
["23:11"]={"The last recorded call on the victim’s cell phone was Sunday night at \003eleven-eleven P.M.\004 Nobody’s seen her since that night.","Vermillion Drift","William Kent Krueger"},
["23:12"]={"There was a confirmatory identification done by undercover officer 6475 at \00323:12\004 hours at the corner of 147th and Amsterdam.","A Naked Singularity","Sergio De La Pava"},
["23:14"]={"When they’d finished their burgers, Melissa glanced at her watch, a big plastic digital thing that looked like it should belong to a child.\n“\003Eleven fourteen\004,” Melissa said. “We’ve still got forty-four minutes to kill before the end of the world.”","The Glass Hotel","Emily St. John Mandel"},
["23:15"]={"\00311:15 p.m.\004 Humph. Mum just rang. “Sorry, darling. It isn’t Newsnight, it’s Breakfast News tomorrow. Could you set it for seven o’clock tomorrow morning, BBC1?”","Bridget Jones’s Diary","Helen Fielding"},
["23:16"]={"Eventually, at \00311:16\004, he did show up, and took his reserved place at the baccarat table. Stephen stopped sipping his tomato juice and Jean-Pierre moved over and waited patiently by the table for one of the men seated on the left or right of Harvey to leave.","Not a Penny More, Not a Penny Less","Jeffrey Archer"},
["23:17"]={"Merral, trying to free his head, glimpsed the time on his helmet datastrip. \00311:17\004:45. Less than a minute. They will be sending out the solar flare warnings now.","The Infinite Day","Chris Walley"},
["23:18"]={"It is \00311:18\004. A row of bungalows in a round with a clump of larch tree in the middle.","Trumpet","Jackie Kay"},
["23:19"]={"A whistle cut sharply across his words. Peter got onto his knees to look out the window, and Miss Fuller glared at him. Polly looked down at her watch: \00311:19\004. The train. But the stationmaster had said it was always late.","Blackout","Connie Willis"},
["23:20"]={"From Balboa Island, he drove south to Laguna Beach. At \003eleven-twenty\004, he parked his van across the street from the Hudston house.","Watchers","Dean Koontz"},
["23:21"]={"The Swedish police did not exactly distinguish themselves. Palme was killed at \00311:21 p.m.\004, but the order to watch the roads didn’t go out until 12:50 and even then the police in patrol cars weren’t told what they were looking for, and the airports were not closed until 1:05 a.m.","Neither Here, Nor There","Bill Bryson"},
["23:22"]={"At \00311:22\004 he handed his ticket to a yawning guard and walked down a long flight of wooden steps to the car-park. A breeze lifted and dropped the leaves of a tree, and he thought of the girl with the blonde hair. His bicycle lay where he had left it.","Dreams of Leaving","Rupert Thomson"},
["23:23"]={"By the time the second lock had also admitted defeat with a click, things had still gone without a hitch. Quinten looked at his watch: \003twenty-three minutes past eleven\004.","The Discovery of Heaven","Harry Mulisch"},
["23:24"]={"\00311:24 P.M.\004\nWillem Voorst was at the controls of the Cessna as they powered through the Aegean night, their heading 210 as they closed rapidly on Andikythera. He was holding their altitude at five hundred meters, their airspeed just under a hundred knots, barely above stall.","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover"},
["23:25"]={"OK, Estelle, I will be at Nice Airport at \00311:25 p.m.\004 on Saturday, BA: Could you send the driver?","Other People’s Money","Justin Cartwright"},
["23:27"]={"At \00311:27 P.M.\004 Jean-Pierre left quietly and returned to the solitude of his hotel room where he remained until 11 A.M. the next day. He phoned no one and did not use room service.","Not a Penny More, Not a Penny Less","Jeffrey Archer"},
["23:29"]={"With a sigh of relief that she had not missed the deadline, she crept between the sheets at \003twenty-nine minutes past eleven\004 and turned out the light at once.","Belle du Seigneur","Albert Cohen"},
["23:30"]={"The ship’s clock in the bar says \003half past eleven\004. Half past eleven is opening time. The hands of the clock have stayed still at half past eleven for fifty years.","Under Milk Wood","Dylan Thomas"},
["23:31"]={"It is \003twenty-nine minutes to midnight\004. Dr. Narlikar’s Nursing Home is running on a skeleton staff; there are many absentees, many employees who have preferred to celebrate the imminent birth of the nation, and will not assist tonight at the births of children.","Midnight’s Children","Salman Rushdie"},
["23:32"]={"This is the evening. This is the night. It is New Year´s Eve. \003In about twenty-eight minutes it will be midnight.\004 I still have twenty-eight minutes left. I have to recollect my thoughts. At twelve o´clock, I should be done thinking.","The Evenings","Gerard Reve"},
["23:33"]={"\00311:33 P.M.\004\nThe storm had cut visuals to a minimum, and the puddle hopper down there was still not responding.","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover"},
["23:34"]={"Reacher retrieved his G36 from under the saloon bar window at \003eleven thirty-four\004 precisely and set out to walk back on the road, which he figured would make the return trip faster.","The Hard Way","Lee Child"},
["23:35"]={"Then at \003eleven thirty-five\004 the door at the rear of the hall opened and a police sergeant and three constables entered, ushered by Bagot.","Hamlet, Revenge!","Michael Innes"},
["23:36"]={"Then Green knocks at the front door at \0032336\004 — Gately has to Log the exact time and then it’s his call whether to unlock the door.","Infinite Jest","David Foster Wallace"},
["23:38"]={"A Ford Focus with the number plate W341 UDG was seen parked close to the house \003between eleven-thirty-five and eleven-forty\004 on the night she died.","The Private Patient","P.D. James"},
["23:39"]={"There’s a whisper down the line at \00311:39\004\nWhen the Night Mail’s ready to depart, Saying “Skimble where is Skimble has he gone to hunt the thimble? We must find him or the train can’t start.”","Old Possum’s Book of Practical Cats","T.S. Eliot"},
["23:40"]={"Grant noticed the time. “It’s \00320 minutes until midnight\004. Who wants to help me hand out glasses and pour champagne?”","Warrior Monk","Ray Keating"},
["23:41"]={"In a little while his mind cleared, but his head ached, arms ached, body ached. The phosphorescent figures on his watch attracted his attention. He peered at them. The time was \00311:41\004. I remember… what do I remember?","Noble House","James Clavell"},
["23:42"]={"At \00311:42\004 then the signal’s nearly due And the passengers are frantic to a man— Then Skimble will appear and he’ll saunter to the rear:","Old Possum’s Book of Practical Cats","T.S. Eliot"},
["23:43"]={"The clock told him it was \003eleven forty-three\004 and in that moment, in a flash of illumination, Mungo understood what the numbers at the end of Moscow Centre’s messages were","Talking to Strange Men","Ruth Rendell"},
["23:45"]={"It was \003fifteen minutes to midnight\004, when the dead—according to Celia—threw off their coffin lids like so many blankets. Stop that, Matt told himself.","The House of the Scorpion","Nancy Farmer"},
["23:46"]={"In the Kismet Lounge, Mr. Early sees suddenly to his horror it’s \00311:46 p.m.\004 He’s been in this place far longer than he’d planned, and he’s had more to drink than he’d planned. Shame! What if, back at the E-Z, his little girl is crying piteously for him?","Doll: A Romance of the Mississippi","Joyce Carol Oates"},
["23:47"]={"If he had glanced at his watch, he would have seen that it was \003thirteen minutes to midnight\004. And if he had been interested in what was going on, he would have heard the voices and bawling of terrified men.","Dead Soldiers Don’t Sing","Rudolf Jašík"},
["23:48"]={"It was \003near midnight\004.\nTorvik took the doll which had been left on the couch in the study, after first having mended its broken foot.","The Hammer of God","Bo Giertz"},
["23:49"]={"Tom shrugged. He pushed his pinkish ruffled sleeve back, and saw that it was \003eleven minutes to midnight\004. Tom finished his coffee.","The Boy Who Followed Ripley","Patricia Highsmith"},
["23:50"]={"At \00311:50 pm\004, I got up extremely quietly, took my things from under the bed, and opened the door one millimeter at a time, so it wouldn’t make any noise.","Extremely Loud and Incredibly Close","Jonathan Safran Foer"},
["23:51"]={"Due at Waterloo at \003eleven-fifty-one\004, panted Smith. “That gives us thirty-nine minutes to get to the other side of the river and reach his hotel.”","The Mystery of Dr. Fu Manchu","Sax Rohmer"},
["23:53"]={"It was \003near midnight\004.\nTorvik took the doll which had been left on the couch in the study, after first having mended its broken foot.","The Hammer of God","Bo Giertz"},
["23:54"]={"His watch read \00311:54 pm\004 Eastern Standard Time. Already it was nearly 6:00 am in Rome. He had left a city frozen by a harsh January storm, after a bleak, wet Christmas season.","Conclave","Greg Tobin"},
["23:55"]={"I am going to lock you in. It is— he consulted his watch, “\003five minutes to midnight\004. Miss Granger, three turns should do it. Good luck.”","Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban","J.K. Rowling"},
["23:56"]={"The human race is at the end of the line, the doomsday clock ticks on. It’s stopped for a decade at \003four minutes to midnight\004, but there the hands still stand. Any minute now they’ll begin to move again.","Wicked Women","Fay Weldon"},
["23:57"]={"Lazara pinned him to the spot with a deathly silence. But she managed to regain her composure \003shortly before midnight\004 and saw him off with a formal kiss.","Twelve pilgrim stories","Gabriel García Márquez"},
["23:58"]={"Humans emerge \003one minute and seventeen seconds before midnight\004. The whole of our recorded history, on this scale, would be no more than a few seconds, a single human lifetime barely an instant.","A Short History of Nearly Everything","Bill Bryson"},
["23:59"]={"Chigurgh rose and picked up the empty casing off the rug and blew into it and put it in his pocket and looked at his watch. The \003new day was still a minute away\004.","No Country for Old Men","Cormac McCarthy"},
}
